  "worked_solution": "The derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=2x+1$,  we have that $f(x+h)=2(x+h)+1.$ Hence,  we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{2(x+h)+1-(2x+1)}{h}).\n$$",
